Enhancement: Add optional reconnect to the SFTP backend

When the SSH connection of the SFTP backend broke during a run, for example
because the server closes connections after a fixed time, restic could not
recover and aborted.

Restic now starts a new SSH connection when the option `-o sftp.reconnect=N`
is set. `N` limits how many reconnects may follow each other less than five
minutes apart. The option is disabled by default. If `ssh` asks for a password,
it asks again on every reconnect and the run waits for the answer.

